    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d293-a2">

                <pb facs="0654" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg606"/>


                <head>Official Notification.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 27, 1867.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Citizens of the United States are informed that, in conjunction with my
                    colleagues, I have made arrangements with the Japanese government by which the
                    city of Yedo, the town of Ne-egata, on the west coast of the harbor of
                    Ebisuminato, on the island of Sado, will be open to them for trade and
                    residence, pursuant to treaty stipulations, on the 1st day of April next.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the
                            United States in Japan,</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
